The explicit inactive-history import gate is refined in
[E-M17-056](milestones.md). This is specification-only acceptance; no import
endpoint, command, journal, consent or worker is implemented by that evidence.
Future targets cover durable exact replay across timeout/restart, current
authorization and private/source physical binding, paused/stopped/lost owners,
capacity, retained cancellation ownership, and native aliases/progress/unknown
receipt preservation. Cached selectors retain their observation-only meaning.
M18.2 remains In progress; configured Codex startup is qualified separately in
E-M17-069 below, while browser/other readers and the full roadmap remain
pending. For E-M17-056, changed-document formatting, canonical validation,
spec-first and progress checks passed with all 310 preceding evidence entries
unchanged. That evidence changed no production or generated contracts, so
functional, Rust, contract and UI lanes were out of scope for that specification
slice.

The private import journal primitive is qualified by [E-M17-057](milestones.md):
exact receipt replay, changed-input conflict, strict catalog validation, private
directory/lock replacement, permissions, symlinks, capacity without eviction,
post-replacement unknown outcome, callback gate retention and selected-file
replacement, and fresh-process receipt durability. The shared private-file
extraction preserves control layout and has direct policy/runtime/CLI consumer
evidence. This does not qualify enrollment, scheduling, HTTP/CLI import, consent
or native publication.

Read-only Codex import preparation has separate focused evidence in
[E-M17-058](milestones.md). It covers complete-record selection, bounded
multi-step reconstruction, stable accepted-prefix reconciliation after append
and process restart, physical/header/profile replacement, rewritten/truncated
prefixes and conservative current context without source admission. This
metadata preparation is not durable acceptance, source consent or scheduling.

The installation-policy import guard is qualified separately in
[E-M17-059](milestones.md): current Admin/configuration/installation and exact
configured journal binding precede receipt lookup, original replay precedes new
revision/selector checks, and live desired runtime state withholds paused,
stopped or lost work. Private control file identity and coordination remain
pinned through settlement. Post-application authority loss is unknown; caller
cancellation retains manager/control/import gates in the blocking operation.
This does not qualify native Write admission, source enrollment, reader-frame
ownership, supervised import scheduling or HTTP/CLI/browser import.

Exact registry import admission has separate evidence in
[E-M17-060](milestones.md), with the complete
`crates/jj-store-capture/tests/source_registry_import.rs` target and its
lease/loss/restart fixtures. It covers unprepared/mismatched selections, current
consent before allocation and selection, unchanged catalogs on preselection
source/authority loss, retained postselection markers, exact replay, capacity,
common aliases and exclusive leases, replacement/header/profile isolation,
append reconciliation without extending history, retained raw-channel handoff,
fresh-process marker reconciliation and withholding rewritten prefixes before
any sanitized cursor. Ordinary active resume cannot borrow an import-only
marker. Existing active admission markers and registry/progress formats remain
supported. This library primitive depends on independently retained durable
intent and policy/Write checks; executable native import admission, owned
scheduling and public HTTP/CLI/browser import remain pending.

Owned import settlement has separate evidence in [E-M17-061](milestones.md) and
`crates/jj-store-server/src/capture_management/tests/import_settlement.rs`. It
retains manager/control/import coordination across an actual native Write
authorization await, resolves original metadata before offered replay bindings,
refuses changed preselection policy/private state, preserves receipts on
postselection authority/runtime/file loss and retains both gates after caller
cancellation until the independently owned operation settles. Existing journal
formats and synchronous callback contracts remain unchanged. This primitive
supplies no source frame, storage lifetime or worker schedule; executable source
enrollment, ingestion and public import remain separate pending gates.

Native source-import composition has separate evidence in
[E-M17-062](milestones.md) and
`crates/jj-store-server/src/capture_management/tests/native_import.rs` with its
ownership fixtures. It proves bounded prefix preparation, actual retained
runtime selection, native Write before durable intent and enrollment, sanitized
publication to current native AgentStore, exact receipt/cursor replay after
append and obsolete selectors, imported parking and raw-channel retention,
changed prefix/physical replacement refusal, policy/runtime revocation and
caller cancellation retaining gates across actual native admission awaits.
Selected intent and import-only markers survive postselection loss without
generic active eligibility or raw persistence. This source-level evidence uses
synthetic qualified Codex records and native MemoryStore, not real
harness/storage/cold qualification. Independent worker/frame/storage scheduling,
public import progress and HTTP/CLI/ browser controls remain pending; this does
not enable configured startup.

Owned source scheduling for JST-COLLAB-017/JST-COLLAB-030 has explicit library
evidence in [E-M17-063](milestones.md),
`crates/jj-store-server/src/capture_management/tests/scheduled_import.rs` and
its handoff/restart fixtures. It selects inactive history into existing retained
source owners and budgets, preserves original intent through lost caller
acknowledgement, bounds the body-free mailbox, renews revocation before
enrollment, refuses another command for an occupied import source, preserves
larger prefix scans across parking, and reconciles original selectors after
runtime restart. Active raw-capacity refusal withholds replacement; compact
active handoff reuses the alias/cursor and keeps one native session. A separate
source-owner regression checks actual raw state before replacing an older cached
compact observation. The executor settlement-hook regression releases step-local
gates only after a cancelled future ends and keeps its original state for
resume. These synthetic Codex/native MemoryStore tests qualify library dispatch
separately from public durable progress/API/CLI/browser, automatic restart
dispatch, real harness/storage and enabled cold startup. M18.2 remains In
progress.

Physical transcript publication inspection additionally qualifies numeric
generation continuation: a later generation receipt cannot hide an earlier
withheld range, a pending continuation retains its prior committed frontier, and
previously unqualified reader history cannot be promoted by a new numeric
generation. Synthetic regressions in the reader publication generation fixture
exercise cross-repository holes, reopen and unrelated physical files. These
results qualify device receipt coverage, not per-request import completion.

Original-import reader association qualification binds actual admitted native
source enrollment to the original receipt ordinal, physical/header witness and
initial reader generation before returning its pipeline. Exact retry, catalog
reopen, missing-association reconstruction and numeric continuation retain the
immutable accepted receipt. Selected file stamps follow synchronized association
replacement under the retained gate. Invalid/foreign/duplicate/changed metadata
withholds, and body-free lookup survives absent transcript files. These
synthetic native MemoryStore/device tests do not qualify public progress or real
harness and RustFS cold startup.

Receipt-backed automatic JSONL publication coverage has separate
JST-COLLAB-018/JST-COLLAB-030 evidence in [E-M17-064](milestones.md) and
`crates/jj-store-capture/tests/reader_publication.rs`, its path/process fixtures
and the owning catalog regressions. It proves cross-repository holes survive
restart; reader acknowledgement and identity-only removal cannot imply native
publication; unknown or mismatched receipts retain the exact Prepared retry;
receipt evidence precedes body removal and is not counted twice after recovery.
A separate process exits after recording a receipt, then a new handle recovers
the same frontier. Corrupt, missing, oversized, foreign, symlinked or public
selected evidence withholds coverage. Ingress refusal selects no requirement;
the finite catalog refuses new ranges without evicting holes, and confirmed
folding frees capacity. Existing history without evidence remains unqualified.
The catalog contains no transcript body, path or native session key. The
existing mixed-reader native recovery regression also proves shared reader
enqueue extends only an already tracked channel, and independent repository
delivery cannot skip its earlier range. These synthetic native-receipt/device
durability tests leave public import phases, HTTP/CLI/browser controls,
accepted-request restart dispatch and real harness/RustFS qualification remain
separate pending gates.

Cached source coverage for JST-COLLAB-017/JST-COLLAB-030 is also extended by
`crates/jj-store-server/tests/capture_management/sources.rs` and the direct
`crates/jj-store-cli/tests/capture_cli/sources.rs` fixtures
([E-M17-055](milestones.md)). The genuine absent-route and cold absent-command
regressions both go from one failure to zero. Bounded cached pages use fresh
runtime generations and monotonically allocated source slots, disclose no
paths/native session IDs/proofs, and admit no historical session. Paused reads
survive transcript-root removal without policy/spool changes. Retained sources
keep their selectors; physical replacement retires a compact slot and allocates
a higher ordinal. Invalid/foreign/beyond-high-water cursors fail closed. Current
Admin/configuration/installation and exact physical journal checks govern reads;
disabled reads create no capture state, while missing enabled observations are
unavailable. Producer-loss, retained gates across caller cancellation and
post-selection authority/physical checks have dedicated private regressions.

The CLI lists one typed page over the explicit loopback endpoint, encodes the
query, validates bounds/order/runtime binding and strict fields, and presents
cached observations safely. Source-stale responses request explicit listing
refresh. This selects no repository/workspace/actor/state directory. Final
focused acceptance passes 46 server library, ten runtime, ten management, 27
supervisor, 14 HTTP, ten capture CLI, ten CLI library, six setup and two local
backend entries in explicit serial execution with original assertions/deadlines.
Four direct packages pass all-target compilation and strict lint after one
mechanical conditional repair. All 183 actual HTTP/SSE responses conform; seven
contract-tool tests, TypeScript fixture and generated web check pass. The
initial HTTP schema assertion and missing runner-governance chapter failures
were repaired and their exact gates pass. Final canonical, boundary,
architecture, progress and formatting checks seal the same change. All 309 prior
parsed evidence entries remain unchanged. This is focused boundary acceptance,
with synthetic qualified headers and MemoryStore; it does not qualify public
enabled startup or real harness/storage operation. Explicit inactive-history
import, browser controls, remaining readers, enabled startup and real
storage/live harness/cold full-flow remain separate qualification gates; M18.2
is In progress and M18.3-M17.7 remain Planned.

Installation capture CLI for JST-COLLAB-017/JST-COLLAB-030 is qualified by
